---
description: Adding params to a method override has no effect. The compiler accepts it, but the callers won’t be able to benefit from the added modifier.
globs:
  - '**/*.cs'
alwaysApply: true
---
# Rule content

Noncompliant code example <pre data-diff-id="1" data-diff-type="noncompliant">
class Base
{
public virtual void Method(int[] numbers)
{
...
}
}
class Derived : Base
{
public override void Method(params int[] numbers) // Noncompliant, method can't be called with params syntax.
{
...
}
}
</pre>
 Compliant solution <pre data-diff-id="1" data-diff-type="compliant">
class Base
{
public virtual void Method(int[] numbers)
{
...
}
}
class Derived : Base
{
public override void Method(int[] numbers)
{
...
}
}
</pre>
